  "blocks": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Something was wrong with Bunny. Her owner, Alexis Devine, had just brought her back from a walk near their home in Tacoma, Washington. Usually, Bunny, a young "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "sheepadoodle",
      "zh": "绵羊贵宾犬"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ", would be tired after the walk. But today, she wouldn’t settle down. For most dog owners, this would be the beginning of an "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "annoying",
      "ref": "v-annoying"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " guessing game. Was Bunny hungry? Did she need to go to the bathroom?"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Devine, however, had a "
     },
     {
      "t": "underline",
      "v": "secret weapon"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ". Bunny walked over to some brightly coloured hexagonal "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "mats",
      "zh": "六边形地垫"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " in the living room and placed her paw on one of the buttons. As a voice said, “Mad”, the dog looked "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "expectantly",
      "ref": "v-expectantly"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " at her owner."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "“Why are you mad?” Devine asked."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Bunny pressed another button, making the mat say, “Ouch.”"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p5",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "“Where ouch?” Devine replied."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p6",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "The dog pressed the buttons for “stranger” and “paw”. Devine checked Bunny’s paws and found the “stranger”: a "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "foxtail spike",
      "zh": "狐尾草尖刺"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p7",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Humans have dreamt of communicating with animals for centuries. Now, with "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "Augmentative and Alternative Communication",
      "zh": "AAC，增强和辅助交流"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " mats like the ones in Bunny’s home, this dream is becoming a "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "reality",
      "ref": "v-reality"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ". Researchers at the University of California, San Diego, are studying around 2,000 dogs worldwide to see how they use the “mats” to express themselves."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p8",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Federico Rossano, the lead researcher, has been surprised by what the animals seem to communicate. Some dogs ask for food "
     },
     {
      "t": "vocab",
      "v": "on behalf of",
      "ref": "v-on-behalf-of"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " other animals in their homes. Some seem to “remember” past events. Cache, a "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "golden retriever",
      "zh": "金毛寻回犬"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ", lives with his owner, Christina Lee. Lee told me that Cache often uses his buttons to talk about past events. Once, Cache’s fur became untidy after he walked through a field of burrs. It took Lee three hours to clean him. Later that day, Cache pressed the button with the name of the field, as well as the one for “worried”."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p9",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "I often wish I could have long, meaningful conversations with my two-year-old tabby, Sushi Two, about her hopes and dreams. I’d also like to find out why she runs around the room at unexpected noises. Disappointingly, however, there are no AAC mats for cats yet. I wonder when my wish will become a reality."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
